## @file
#  MemoryMapLib for the MediaTek MT6877.
#
#  SCAFFOLD ONLY: never built. The .inf format follows what UEFI-PLAN.md:52
#  reports of stonePkg's 15-line MemoryMapLib.inf, but no edk2 tree was present
#  to check it against, and LIBRARY_CLASS below is a guess: UEFI-PLAN.md does not
#  say what class Mu-Silicium binds MemoryMapLib as.
#
#  TODO: confirm LIBRARY_CLASS against stonePkg/Library/MemoryMapLib/MemoryMapLib.inf.
#        It is likely a Silicon-specific class name, which is why the class has to
#        be declared in MT6877Pkg.dec (the LibraryClasses stanza there is commented
#        out for exactly this reason).
#
#  TODO: this scaffold's MemoryMapLib.c declares its own struct and accessors
#        (Mt6877GetMemoryRegions etc.) that no other module calls. That is not
#        what Mu-Silicium's MemoryMapLib does: its callers asked for the map by
#        region NAME (UEFI-PLAN.md:1c). If the real interface is a
#        name -> address lookup, this .inf is still right (same sources, same
#        consumer) and only the .c's API is wrong.
##

